          "content": "**Decision:** **Approve recommendation (`waive_late_fee`)**\n\n**Instruction to Reviewer:**  \nProceed with applying the **$60 late fee waiver** to Jordan Kim\u2019s account and issue the supportive communication as outlined in your proposal.\n\n---\n\n### **Management Rationale**\n\n1. **Policy Alignment & Legitimate Hardship:**  \n   Jordan Kim\u2019s sudden, documented one-week hospitalization clearly meets our policy criteria for an involuntary hardship exception. Given an otherwise clean record (only one late payment), there is virtually no risk of policy abuse.\n\n2. **Retention Value vs. Cost Control Metrics:**  \n   While our departmental scorecard emphasizes cost control and efficiency this quarter, cost control must be balanced against customer lifetime value (LTV). Alienating a reliable, active account holder over an isolated $60 fee risks customer churn; acquiring a replacement customer costs significantly more than the one-time concession. \n\n3. **Operational Efficiency:**  \n   First-contact resolution minimizes repeat inquiries, supervisor escalations, and administrative overhead, directly supporting our operational efficiency goals. \n\n### **Next Steps**\n* Process the $60 adjustment under the standard hardship waiver code.\n* Send the customer confirmation wishing them a smooth recovery.\n* Log the exception clearly in the account CRM notes for future reference.",
